# Code owners for Halonic.
#
# Informational only. GitHub doesn't let an account approve its own pull
# request, so code-owner review is not a required check. Each package names
# its owner in its own package.json ("halonic": { "owner" }) and AGENTS.md;
# this file only routes review requests.
#
# The maintainers team is created when the repository goes public.

* @halonic-com/maintainers

# The rules below override the line above for these paths.
# Files whose change needs a maintainer to approve, not just a green check.
# Turn on "Require review from Code Owners" in the branch ruleset for main
# for this to block a merge.

# The list of phrases the personal-terms guard ignores: widening it hides
# text from the guard.
/tooling/check/terms-allowed-phrases.txt @halonic-com/maintainers

# The leak guard and the files that decide how it runs. CI runs the guard from
# the base commit, so a change here only takes effect once an owner has agreed.
/.github/CODEOWNERS @halonic-com/maintainers
/.github/workflows/ @halonic-com/maintainers
/.github/actions/ @halonic-com/maintainers
/tooling/check/src/leaks/ @halonic-com/maintainers
/tooling/check/src/cli/leaks.ts @halonic-com/maintainers
/tooling/check/leak-allow.txt @halonic-com/maintainers
